  "result": "I added `formatBytes(n)` in `src/cli/bytes.ts` and a node:test file at `test/cli/bytes.test.ts`, and committed both as `fad4581`. The new tests pass, and `tsc --noEmit` and biome are clean on the new files. I did not run the full `npm test` or `npm run gate`.\n\n- **Formatting:** it renders B, KiB, MiB or GiB with one decimal, for example `1536` gives `1.5 KiB`. GiB is the top unit, so very large values stay in GiB (5 TiB prints as `5120.0 GiB`).\n- **Rounding:** a value that rounds up to 1024 moves to the next unit, so `1024 ** 2 - 1` gives `1.0 MiB` rather than `1024.0 KiB`.\n- **Negatives:** they keep a minus sign, for example `-1536` gives `-1.5 KiB`.\n- **Non-finite input:** `NaN` or `Infinity` returns the value followed by ` B`. You didn't specify this case, so say if you want different handling.",
